{"obligations":[{"id":"D1","kind":"entity","role":"declaration","statement":"Input contains events with string group, integer time and integer-or-null value, integer start and end with start<=end, positive integer width, and fill equal to 'none' or 'previous'. Output is a JSON-compatible list of records with group,start,count,value.","required":true,"scope":["input and output"],"dependencies":[],"acceptance_criteria":["Preserve the specified input domain and output fields.","Return a JSON-serializable value."],"sources":[{"quote":"Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Input structure and domain."},{"quote":"Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Output structure."},{"quote":"Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"JSON compatibility."},{"quote":"The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Serialization boundary."}]},{"id":"O1","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"Provide a pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data) function in solution.py.","required":true,"scope":["implementation and valid invocations"],"dependencies":[],"acceptance_criteria":["solution.py exposes solve(data).","Equivalent inputs produce equivalent outputs.","The function is pure."],"sources":[{"quote":"Implement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Module and function contract."},{"quote":"Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Language, purity and determinism."}]},{"id":"S1","kind":"safety_property","role":"guarantee","statement":"Use only the Python standard library and perform no external I/O.","required":true,"scope":["implementation and execution"],"dependencies":[],"acceptance_criteria":["No third-party libraries are required.","No external I/O occurs."],"sources":[{"quote":"Use Python standard library only, no external I/O.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Dependency and I/O restrictions."},{"quote":"Use only the standard library, no external I/O.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Repeated restriction."}]},{"id":"O2","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"Enumerate all unique event group names lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events. For each group emit buckets at start+k*width for nonnegative integers k strictly below end, covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)). Return records in group then ascending bucket order.","required":true,"scope":["all valid inputs"],"dependencies":[{"id":"D1","relation":"uses_definition"}],"acceptance_criteria":["Groups equal the sorted set of all event group names.","Bucket starts are exactly start+k*width<end for k>=0.","Intervals include their left boundary and exclude their clipped right boundary.","start=end produces no records.","Empty events produces no records.","Records contain group,start,count,value in the specified group then bucket order."],"sources":[{"quote":"Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Complete group enumeration."},{"quote":"For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,...","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Bucket progression."},{"quote":"strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Bucket boundaries."},{"quote":"Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Record structure and ordering."},{"quote":"Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Exact structural and ordering contract."}]},{"id":"O3","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"For each group and bucket, count every event occurrence in that group whose time lies in the bucket and whose value is non-null, and sum precisely those values. Duplicate occurrences contribute separately. A bucket is nonempty exactly when count>0, and its output value then equals the sum.","required":true,"scope":["each emitted bucket"],"dependencies":[{"id":"O2","relation":"uses_proof"}],"acceptance_criteria":["count equals the number of qualifying non-null event occurrences.","Null and out-of-range values contribute neither count nor sum.","Duplicates contribute separately.","For count>0, value equals the sum, including zero and negative sums."],"sources":[{"quote":"Sum only non-null in-range values;","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Aggregation eligibility."},{"quote":"count counts these values.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Count eligibility."},{"quote":"A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Nonempty output value."},{"quote":"Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Zero and duplicate semantics."}]},{"id":"I1","kind":"invariant","role":"guarantee","statement":"Within each group, previous starts absent and after each bucket equals the sum of the latest nonempty emitted bucket processed so far, if one exists. Nonempty buckets update previous, including zero sums; empty buckets preserve it. Events before start never seed previous.","required":true,"scope":["bucket traversal within each group"],"dependencies":[{"id":"O3","relation":"uses_proof"}],"acceptance_criteria":["Previous is independent for each group.","Only nonempty emitted buckets update previous.","Zero remains a present previous value.","Empty buckets never reset previous.","Pre-start events never seed previous."],"sources":[{"quote":"A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Previous update."},{"quote":"empty buckets never reset previous.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Previous preservation."},{"quote":"Events before start never seed previous.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Causal initialization boundary."},{"quote":"Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Zero is a valid previous sum."},{"quote":"For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,...","origin":"inferred","interpretation":"Previous belongs to the group being traversed.","justification":"The requested per-group aggregation entails independent previous values across groups."}]},{"id":"O4","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"A bucket with count zero has null value for fill='none'. For fill='previous', its value is the latest preceding nonempty bucket sum within that group, or null before the first nonempty bucket.","required":true,"scope":["empty emitted buckets"],"dependencies":[{"id":"I1","relation":"uses_proof"},{"id":"O3","relation":"uses_proof"}],"acceptance_criteria":["Empty buckets retain count zero regardless of fill.","fill='none' gives null for every empty bucket.","fill='previous' gives the latest previous nonempty sum, including zero.","Before the first nonempty bucket, fill='previous' gives null."],"sources":[{"quote":"Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first);","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Empty bucket fill behavior."}]},{"id":"O5","kind":"postcondition","role":"guarantee","statement":"Match both public examples exactly: cancelling a events produce count 2 and value 0 at start 0, then count-zero buckets at 2 and 4 filled with 0; the pre-start z event yields a count-zero bucket at 0 with null value.","required":true,"scope":["public example inputs"],"dependencies":[{"id":"O2","relation":"uses_proof"},{"id":"O3","relation":"uses_proof"},{"id":"O4","relation":"uses_proof"}],"acceptance_criteria":["For a events (0,2),(1,-2), start=0,end=5,width=2,fill='previous', return [{group:'a',start:0,count:2,value:0},{group:'a',start:2,count:0,value:0},{group:'a',start:4,count:0,value:0}].","For z event (-1,9), start=0,end=1,width=2,fill='previous', return [{group:'z',start:0,count:0,value:null}]."],"sources":[{"quote":"Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Examples are acceptance cases."},{"quote":"Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Zero propagation in the first example."},{"quote":"Events before start never seed previous.","origin":"explicit","interpretation":"Pre-start exclusion in the second example."}]}],"category_review":{"entities":"Structured events input, range, width, fill mode, and ordered output records.","preconditions":"No separately stated caller assumptions; D1 declares the input domain.","postconditions":"Pure deterministic callable, enumeration, aggregation, filling, exact ordering and public examples.","invariants":"Independent per-group previous sums update only on nonempty buckets, including zero.","safety_properties":"Standard library only and no external I/O.","liveness_properties":"None stated.","resource_constraints":"None stated.","error_semantics":"Invalid-input behavior is unspecified.","explicit_non_goals":"None stated.","ambiguities":"None requiring resolution within the specified input domain."},"clauses":[{"clause_id":"C1","quote":"Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling","disposition":"context","refs":[],"note":"Task title."},{"clause_id":"C2","quote":"Implement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C3","quote":"Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C4","quote":"Use Python standard library only, no external I/O.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["S1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C5","quote":"Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C6","quote":"Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C7","quote":"For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,...","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O2","I1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C8","quote":"strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C9","quote":"Sum only non-null in-range values;","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O3"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C10","quote":"count counts these values.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O3"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C11","quote":"A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O3","I1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C12","quote":"Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first);","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O4"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C13","quote":"empty buckets never reset previous.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["I1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C14","quote":"Events before start never seed previous.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["I1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C15","quote":"Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C16","quote":"Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O3","I1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C17","quote":"Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C18","quote":"Use only the standard library, no external I/O.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["S1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C19","quote":"The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C20","quote":"Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.","disposition":"obligations","refs":["D1","O2"],"note":""},{"clause_id":"C21","quote":"Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]","disposition":"obligations","refs":["O5"],"note":"Examples constrain zero propagation and pre-start exclusion; held-out scoring is evaluation context."}],"assumptions":[],"ambiguities":[],"selected_defaults":[]}